<title>ESTONIA: ESTONIA-MERGED UHISPANK TO CUT 250 JOBS.</title>
<headline>ESTONIA-MERGED UHISPANK TO CUT 250 JOBS.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Uhispank, after the merger with Pohja Eesti Pank, will cut 250 existing employees, the bank said on Monday.</p>
<p>At present Uhispank has 800 employees and PEP has 430 staff, but the banks forecast that they need only 1,000 employees, the bank said in a statement.</p>
<p>The bank plans to keep the best employees from both banks, the bank added.</p>
<p>Uhispank's share holder meeting will be held on April 12 and will decide on the merger proposal. The merged bank will be the second largest bank in Estonia.</p>
<p>-- David Mardiste Tallinn newsroom +372 630 8400 reuters@reuters.ee</p>
</text>
